---
// Spec-driven development (R066–R069 as shipped): the problem, without/with, four steps with real examples.
const without = [
  'Intent lives in chat history and is gone next session',
  'The agent rebuilds how a feature works from old tasks',
  '"Done" is the agent\'s word for it',
  'Docs drift until nobody trusts them',
]
const withVibeDoc = [
  'Each capability has one spec: requirements with WHEN/THEN scenarios',
  'The agent sees the related requirements when it claims a task',
  "Scenarios seed each task's checklist, and the epic shows which ones passed",
  'A finished epic merges its spec changes in one reviewed diff',
]
const pre = 'm-0 mt-4 flex-1 overflow-x-auto bg-ink px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs leading-[1.65] whitespace-pre-wrap text-[#e8e8f0]'
---
<section id="sdd" aria-labelledby="sdd-heading" class="mx-auto flex max-w-[1200px] flex-col gap-12 px-5 pt-28 pb-12 sm:px-8">
  <div class="vd-reveal flex max-w-[760px] flex-col gap-4">
    <p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.08em] text-violet-ink uppercase">Spec-driven development</p>
    <h2 id="sdd-heading" class="m-0 text-[40px] leading-[1.04] font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] sm:text-[52px]">Vibe coding forgets. Specs remember.</h2>
    <p class="m-0 text-lg leading-relaxed text-body">
      In a chat, what you asked for scrolls away and "done" means "trust me". VibeDoc keeps what each feature must do as
      living specs next to your code, turns the promises into checks, and verifies the work against them before you approve it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="vd-reveal grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(320px,100%),1fr))] gap-4">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3.5 rounded-xl border border-rule bg-surface p-7">
      <h3 class="m-0 font-mono text-xs font-normal text-pencil">Without specs</h3>
      <ul class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-3.5 p-0">
        {without.map((t) => <li class="text-base leading-normal text-body"><span aria-hidden="true">✕ </span>{t}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3.5 rounded-xl border border-violet/45 bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_0_0_4px_rgba(124,106,247,0.08)]">
      <h3 class="m-0 font-mono text-xs font-normal text-violet-ink">With VibeDoc</h3>
      <ul class="m-0 flex list-none flex-col gap-3.5 p-0">
        {withVibeDoc.map((t) => <li class="text-base leading-normal"><span aria-hidden="true">✓ </span>{t}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ol aria-label="Spec-driven, step by step" class="m-0 grid list-none grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(270px,100%),1fr))] gap-4 p-0">
    <li class="vd-reveal flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-rule bg-surface">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 px-5 pt-5"><p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs text-pencil">1 · Capability spec</p><h3 class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold">What it does today</h3></div>
      <pre class={pre}><span class="text-[#8c8ca0]">docs/specs/memory.md</span>
<span class="text-[#aaa0fa]">### Requirement:</span> Session budget
Session start SHALL fit the
memory budget.

<span class="text-[#aaa0fa]">#### Scenario:</span> Many entries
- WHEN there are 200 entries
- THEN only what fits is listed</pre>
    </li>
    <li class="vd-reveal flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-rule bg-surface">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 px-5 pt-5"><p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs text-pencil">2 · Epic</p><h3 class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold">What will change, and how we'll know</h3></div>
      <pre class={pre}><span class="text-[#8c8ca0]">plans/roadmap/R069-….md</span>
<span class="text-[#aaa0fa]">## Scenarios</span>
### S1: Bigger budget
- WHEN 300 entries exist
- THEN session start still fits

<span class="text-[#aaa0fa]">## Spec changes</span>
#### MODIFIED Requirement:
Session budget</pre>
    </li>
    <li class="vd-reveal flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-rule bg-surface">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 px-5 pt-5"><p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs text-pencil">3 · Verify</p><h3 class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold">Checked against what was asked</h3></div>
      <div class="m-5 mb-5 flex flex-1 flex-col gap-2.5">
        <p class="m-0 rounded-md border-l-[3px] border-[#d64545] bg-[#fdf2f2] px-3 py-2.5 text-[13px] leading-normal"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-[#b42f2f]">critical</span><br />AC2 "Unknown plan → 400": route returns 500</p>
        <p class="m-0 rounded-md border-l-[3px] border-[#c46a1f] bg-[#fdf5ed] px-3 py-2.5 text-[13px] leading-normal"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-[#9a520f]">major</span><br />S1 has no test step</p>
        <p class="m-0 mt-auto text-[13px] text-pencil">Tick findings → <b class="text-ink">Send back 2 findings</b></p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="vd-reveal flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-rule bg-surface">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 px-5 pt-5"><p class="m-0 font-mono text-xs text-pencil">4 · Merge</p><h3 class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold">The spec stays current</h3></div>
      <pre class={pre}><span class="text-[#8c8ca0]">Merge R069 into the spec</span>
<span class="text-[#f08c8c]">− fit 2000 tokens</span>
<span class="text-[#5fd6b4]">+ fit 3000 tokens</span>
<span class="text-[#f08c8c]">− WHEN 200 entries</span>
<span class="text-[#5fd6b4]">+ WHEN 300 entries</span>

<span class="mt-1.5 inline-block rounded-md bg-violet px-3 py-1 text-night">Accept</span></pre>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="vd-reveal m-0 max-w-[820px] text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-body">
    Brownfield-first: you never write specs for the whole codebase up front. A spec starts with the first epic that touches a
    feature and grows with every epic after it, the same delta idea OpenSpec uses (ADDED, MODIFIED, REMOVED, RENAMED).
  </p>
</section>
